[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Static Code Analysis and Code Quality Gates in CI/CD"},{"order":2,"type":"subheading","text":"Introduction"},{"order":3,"type":"paragraph","text":"Integrating static code analysis and quality gates into your CI/CD pipeline ensures that security vulnerabilities, code smells, and technical debt are identified and addressed before code reaches production. Tools like SonarQube and Checkmarx automate this validation process."},{"order":4,"type":"subheading","text":"Key Concepts"},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Static Application Security Testing (SAST): Analyzing source code for vulnerabilities without executing it."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Code Smells: Maintainability issues that make code confusing or difficult to maintain."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Quality Gates: A set of threshold conditions (e.g., zero critical vulnerabilities, minimum 80% test coverage) that a build must meet to pass."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Jenkins Pipeline Integration Example"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Below is an example of a Jenkinsfile incorporating a SonarQube analysis stage and quality gate check."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"pipeline {
    agent any
    stages {
        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                sh 'mvn clean package'
            }
        }
        stage('SonarQube Analysis') {
            steps {
                script {
                    def scannerHome = tool 'SonarQubeScanner'
                    withSonarQubeEnv('SonarQubeServer') {
                        sh "${scannerHome}/bin/sonar-scanner"
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        stage('Quality Gate') {
            steps {
                timeout(time: 10, unit: 'MINUTES') {
                    waitForQualityGate abortPipeline: true
                }
            }
        }
    }
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices"},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Run analysis early in the pipeline to provide fast feedback to developers."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Define strict quality gates for production branches while allowing incremental improvements for legacy codebases."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Regularly review and suppress false positives to maintain trust in the automated metrics."}]
